---
import CalculatorLayout from '../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import SmuGpaCalculatorWidget from '../components/calculators/SmuGpaCalculator';

const relatedCalculators = [
  { title: "NUS CAP Calculator", path: "/nus-cap-calculator" },
  { title: "NTU CGPA Calculator", path: "/ntu-cgpa-calculator" },
  { title: "SUSS GPA Calculator", path: "/suss-gpa-calculator" },
];
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="SMU GPA Calculator"
  description="Calculate your Grade Point Average (GPA) for Singapore Management University (SMU). Supports the 4.0 (with 4.3 A+) grading system and Latin Honours."
  category="Academic & Education"
  categoryPath="/categories/academic"
>
  <SmuGpaCalculatorWidget client:load slot="calculator" />

  <Fragment slot="content">
    <h2>How to use the SMU GPA Calculator</h2>
    <p>
      The <strong>SMU GPA Calculator</strong> is tailored specifically for the unique grading system at Singapore Management University. While SMU's maximum official GPA is capped at 4.0, an A+ grade carries a weight of 4.3 grade points, which can help offset lower grades in other courses.
    </p>
    <p>
      To use the calculator:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>(Optional) Enter your current standing:</strong> Input your current Cumulative GPA and the total number of Course Units (CUs) you have completed. Note that SMU often uses 0.5 or 1.0 CUs per course.</li>
      <li><strong>Add your current courses:</strong> For each course, enter the CUs and your expected grade.</li>
      <li><strong>Pass/Fail Options:</strong> If a course is taken on a Pass/Fail basis, select 'P' or 'F (Pass/Fail)'. These will not affect your GPA.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The tool will automatically display your expected GPA and your projected Latin Honours classification based on SMU's official guidelines.
    </p>

    <h3>SMU Grade Points Table</h3>
    <p>SMU uses a unique 4.0 grading system where an A+ gives you extra points (4.3) to act as a buffer:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>A+:</strong> 4.3</li>
      <li><strong>A:</strong> 4.0</li>
      <li><strong>A-:</strong> 3.7</li>
      <li><strong>B+:</strong> 3.3</li>
      <li><strong>B:</strong> 3.0</li>
      <li><strong>B-:</strong> 2.7</li>
      <li><strong>C+:</strong> 2.3</li>
      <li><strong>C:</strong> 2.0</li>
      <li><strong>C-:</strong> 1.7</li>
      <li><strong>D+:</strong> 1.3</li>
      <li><strong>D:</strong> 1.0</li>
      <li><strong>F:</strong> 0.0</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>SMU Latin Honours Classification</h3>
    <p>SMU awards Latin Honours based on your final cumulative GPA:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Summa Cum Laude (Highest Distinction):</strong> GPA 3.80 - 4.00</li>
      <li><strong>Magna Cum Laude (High Distinction):</strong> GPA 3.60 - 3.79</li>
      <li><strong>Cum Laude (Distinction):</strong> GPA 3.40 - 3.59</li>
      <li><strong>High Merit:</strong> GPA 3.00 - 3.39</li>
      <li><strong>Merit:</strong> GPA 2.50 - 2.99</li>
    </ul>
    <p><em>Note: You need a minimum GPA of 2.0 to graduate.</em></p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          Why does A+ give 4.3 points if the max GPA is 4.0?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          At SMU, the maximum cumulative GPA you can graduate with is capped at 4.0. However, an A+ grade awards 4.3 grade points during calculation. This means an A+ can help offset a lower grade (like an A- or B+) to bring your average back up to a 4.0.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          How do I handle 0.5 CU courses?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          Our calculator allows decimal inputs for Course Units. Simply enter '0.5' in the CUs field for half-credit courses.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          Do Pass/Fail courses affect Latin Honours?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          Pass/Fail courses do not affect your GPA calculation. However, you should check SMU's official guidelines, as there may be limits on the total number of Pass/Fail courses you can take while remaining eligible for certain Honours classifications.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="related">
    {relatedCalculators.map(calc => (
      <li>
        <a href={calc.path} class="group flex items-center p-2 rounded-md hover:bg-white dark:hover:bg-slate-700 transition-colors">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2 text-slate-400 group-hover:text-teal-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 group-hover:text-teal-600 dark:group-hover:text-teal-400">{calc.title}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>
